INSERT INTO public.reading_sets (
    set_id, title, title_zh, grade, difficulty, topic, passage,
    word_count, estimated_minutes, sort_order, version, updated_at
) VALUES (
    'r08-01',
    $seedie$Our School Garden Project$seedie$,
    $seedie$我们的校园花园项目$seedie$,
    8,
    $seedie$medium$seedie$,
    $seedie$school_life$seedie$,
    $seedie$Last spring, Class 8A started a small garden behind the school library. At first, the ground was hard and full of dry leaves. Nobody believed plants could grow there. Then Ms. Chen, our science teacher, brought tools, seeds, and a simple plan.

Every Tuesday afternoon, ten students worked in teams. One team cleaned the soil. Another team built wooden boxes for vegetables. A third team wrote labels with both English and Chinese names. We planted tomatoes, lettuce, and sunflowers. We also kept a garden diary. In the diary, we wrote the date, the weather, and what we did that day.

The work was not always easy. One week, heavy rain washed away some young plants. Another week, insects ate the lettuce leaves. Ms. Chen did not give us the answers at once. She asked, "What can we try next?" So we searched online, talked with the school gardener, and tried new ideas. We covered the soil with dry grass to keep water in. We also planted flowers that insects do not like near the lettuce.

By June, the garden looked green and lively. We <<harvested>> the first tomatoes and shared them with teachers. More importantly, we learned that science is not only in textbooks. It is also about careful observation, patience, and working together. Now other classes want to join the project next term.$seedie$,
    248,
    8,
    0,
    1,
    2026072901
)
